      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "Continuing on the topic of sensory overload, one of the most common coping
    mechanisms for autistic individuals is stimming\u2014a term for self-stimulatory
    behaviors. Stimming involves repetitive movements, sounds, or actions that can
    serve as both a distraction and a form of self-soothing. Common examples include
    hand-flapping, \nrocking, and echolalia (repeating words or phrases)."
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
